"""Framework defaults for every piece of human-facing text a generated file contains.

One mechanism for all of it: a pack supplies `Pack.text`, a flat mapping from these keys to
its own wording, and `Pack.say(key, **fields)` looks the key up there first and here second.
The key set is the contract. The values below are deliberately plain English, so an
unconfigured pack produces something legible and obviously unlocalised rather than text in
a language this repository has no business choosing.

Values are `str.format` templates. A pack may reorder or drop fields, but not invent them.
"""

from __future__ import annotations

from collections.abc import Mapping

